    },
    {
      "id": "Wh5fG7K2V0r105nnoKfgl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 259.0889893461158,
      "y": 1331.2429740576097,
      "width": 846.9187622070312,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1363716934,
      "version": 1180,
      "versionNonce": 1085608756,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781960928994,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The solution tells us the scales of column #1 plus column #2 that will lead to the vector on\nright-hand side. In this example, it's move 1 unit of column vector #1 from the origin and then \nmove 2 units of column vector #2.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The solution tells us the scales of column #1 plus column #2 that will lead to the vector on\nright-hand side. In this example, it's move 1 unit of column vector #1 from the origin and then \nmove 2 units of column vector #2.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "GMSWrbuz6CF7CS10nxrPO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 269.4232178617408,
      "y": 1865.6570365576097,
      "width": 903.5387573242188,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aYV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 770230918,
      "version": 1730,
      "versionNonce": 1687456948,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1781960928994,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So finding solution of the system of equations is just like finding the combination of the scales.\nThat's why it's called linear combination.\n\nAlso, using Column Picture makes our life easier when dealing with n dimensions while it's \nimpossible to use Row Picture to conceptualise if it comes to higher dimension which is not scalable.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So finding solution of the system of equations is just like finding the combination of the scales.\nThat's why it's called linear combination.\n\nAlso, using Column Picture makes our life easier when dealing with n dimensions while it's \nimpossible to use Row Picture to conceptualise if it comes to higher dimension which is not scalable.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
